"Boudewijn Waijers" <kroisos@REMOVETHIS.home.nl> writes:
> Jukka Lahtinen wrote:

> >> wb to wield short sword.
> >> x to make it secondary.
> >> wa to wield katana as primary.
> >> #tw to use both.
> 
> Note that you have to repeat this sequence every time you want to
> #twoweapon again, for example after you've used your pickaxe.

Not as long as you don't change your secondary weapon.
When I start twoweaponing, the secondary weapon usually stays in my
secondary hand if I temporarily wield something else in my primary hand
for some reason.
Then, to change back, I just rewield the primary weapon and #tw again.

> Hence, it would be wise to first put "pushweapon" in your options file. If
> you do so, the above gets one command shorter every time you use it:
> wb to wield short sword.
> wa to wield katana as primary AND make the short sword secondary
> #tw to use both.

Yeah, but with pushweapon, EVERY time you wield something else in your
primary weapon hand, unless you first wield nothing, the secondary weapon
also gets changed and you have to first rewield the intended secondary
weapon, then the primary weapon, and then #tw.

When #twoweaponing and the pushweapon option were introduced to the game,
I tried that for a while but soon realized I prefer having pushweapon off,
so there will often be less weapon management needed.
Of course, this is a matter of preference and YMMV.

